              aligned   partial
  p1          22/24     7/36
  p2          22/24     10/36
  p3          21/24     11/36
  p7          24/24     34/36                       -> 151/240

**p7 is essentially production-clean**: 45/45 on real content across all three
corpora, 24/24 on aligned geometry, 34/36 on partial. Its two misses are
`screen` q48 at 72x88 and 80x88 — now pinned, and p7 is in the dims gate.

p1/p2/p3 divergences land in exactly the classes p0/p4 already showed, with NO
new class and NO new image: every real-content miss is `1028637.png` (the CID22
RD near-tie band) or `graph.png` (the #71 screen band); every ALIGNED dims miss
is `screen` at q48 on 256/384/512; the partial-dims misses are the documented
presets-0..5 partial-SB structural gap. Magnitudes -1.6%..+1.5%, both
directions.

