  read these before reading any pass rate.

Regenerate with `python3 tools/coverage_matrix.py` (add --csv for a machine
form). It consolidates every benchmarks/identity_full_8bit*.tsv and prints
`--` for an axis with NO cells, because a missing cell count is a coverage
claim nobody tested and that is more dangerous than a failing one.

### What the completed matrix establishes

- **Presets 5 and 8..13 are byte-identical to C on REAL content — photo AND
  screen, 225/225 across p5/p8/p9/p11/p12** (the p6/p7/p10/p13 columns were
  already clean). Together with p6/p7 that makes **every preset >= 5
  production-clean on real content**.
- **Every preset >= 6 is 24/24 on aligned geometry and 34-36/36 on partial**;
  p8/p10/p11/p12 are a clean 36/36. The dims gate default is therefore widened
  from {6,9,13} to ALL of 6..13 — measured per preset, not assumed to follow a
  neighbour.
- **The remaining gap is presets 0..4 only**, and it is the two known classes:
  partial-SB geometry (7-12/36; presets 0-5 skip the C-faithful PD1 walk on a
  non-aligned SB) and screen/photo RD near-ties on two specific images.
- **p5 is the transition**: 24/24 aligned, 25/36 partial (vs 7-12/36 for p0-p4)
  and 45/45 on real content. Finer-grained than the docs' "presets 0-5" band.

Default gate run after widening: **1036/1036 + 4 pinned, 0 harness errors.**

## UPDATE 2026-08-04 — two of the four pins promoted (this file's TSVs are now
## two rows stale)

`screen 64 64 63 1` (C 64 B, port 71 B) and `screen 128 128 63 1` (C 185 B,
port 193 B) — the #71 palette-over-picking pins recorded above — are now
byte-IDENTICAL and have been promoted out of `KNOWN_DIFF`. Root cause: the MDS3
independent-uv chroma rewrite in `leaf_funnel.rs` rebuilt every candidate's uv
fast rate with `palette_uv_mode_fac_bits[0][0]`, including LUMA-PALETTE
candidates, which C prices with the `[1][0]` row — C's recompute there is
`svt_aom_get_intra_uv_fast_rate(pcs, ctx, cand_bf, 1)` on the REAL candidate
(`update_intra_chroma_mode`, product_coding_loop.c:7095; the row is chosen by
`use_palette_y = cand->palette_info && palette_size[0] > 0`, rd_cost.c:518-520).
That under-costed a palette candidate's chroma flag at every `ind_uv_last_mds`
preset (M1..M5) and tipped the palette-vs-regular RD tie toward palette.

Re-measured 2026-08-04 on the same host/oracle:

  default gate (synthetic + dims)  **1038 / 1038 byte-identical, +2 pinned,
                                   0 harness errors** (was 1036/1036 + 4)
  cells whose port bytes moved     2 — exactly the two promoted cells
  real tier (IF_TIER=real, 450)    403 IDENTICAL / 47 DIFFERS, unchanged;
                                   6 already-DIFFERS preset-4 cells shifted
                                   bytes, none flipped either way

Anti-vacuity, run both ways: with the fix reverted the two cells report
`UNEXPECTED DIVERGENCES  screen 64 64 63 1 [C=64 port=71]` /
`screen 128 128 63 1 [C=185 port=193]` (0/2); restored, 2/2.

The two remaining pins (`screen 72 88 48 7`, `screen 80 88 48 7`) are unchanged.
